Fixed.

## Diagnosis

The bug was in `wrap_bare_frontmatter()` in `crates/liwe/src/markdown.rs`.

Bare frontmatter is implemented by wrapping the detected leading header block in `---` fences before handing it to `pulldown-cmark`. The wrapper was cleaning the header by dropping every line that started with a space:

```rust
.filter(|l| !l.starts_with(' '))
```

That preserved scalar fields like:

```yaml
title: Task A
status: ready
```

but destroyed valid indented YAML sequence items:

```yaml
depends:
  - foo
  - bar
```

After cleaning, the metadata became effectively:

```yaml
depends:
```

So `find --meta depends=foo` could not match. Fenced YAML worked because it bypassed this bare-frontmatter wrapper.

## Fix

Changed the wrapper to preserve YAML indentation and only trim trailing whitespace from the detected header block:

```rust
let cleaned_header = header.trim_end();
```

This keeps sequence items intact while still avoiding extra trailing blank content inside the synthetic frontmatter fence.

## Regression test

Added `value_in_bare_yaml_sequence_matches` in:

```text
crates/liwe/tests/find_metadata_test.rs
```

It verifies that a bare-frontmatter document with:

```yaml
title: Task A
depends:
  - foo
  - bar
```

matches:

```rust
metadata_filters: vec![("depends".to_string(), "foo".to_string())]
```

## Verification

Ran:

```bash
cargo test -p liwe value_in_bare_yaml_sequence_matches --test find_metadata_test
cargo test
```

Both pass. Working tree contains only:

